// Type-checking for scripts/, which svelte-check does not cover.
//
// The generated .svelte-kit/tsconfig.json's `include` lists only src, test,
// tests and the vite configs — so scripts/run-pipeline.ts, the ingestion
// pipeline that runs in production every 15 minutes, had ZERO type coverage in
// CI. It could have been broken by any change to src/lib/server/* and nothing
// would have said so until a scheduled run failed.
//
// This is a SEPARATE config rather than an `include` override on the root
// tsconfig on purpose. TypeScript replaces `include` across `extends` instead of
// merging it, so covering scripts from the root would mean copying SvelteKit's
// generated list and keeping that copy in step with it by hand — a copy that
// goes stale silently, under-checking the app while still reporting success.
// This repo has already been bitten three times by configuration that quietly
// did nothing (duplicate migration versions making `supabase db reset` a no-op,
// this very include, and sharp's exports map hiding its own types); one source
// of truth per scope is cheaper than a fourth.
//
// compilerOptions are inherited from the root config so the two agree on
// strictness. Only the file set differs. Scripts import from src/ with relative
// paths and use no $lib alias, so nothing else is needed.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noEmit": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["scripts/**/*.ts"]
}
